[49m[38;5;10m+     1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # CONFIGS.md — Configuration-surface table (Phase A, gate for Phase B)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Derived mechanically from the C source: the axes below are the ones the C code
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m actually distinguishes, not the ones that look interesting.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Mechanical derivation of the axes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Public entry points** — the full set, from `c_src/include/lib.h`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | entry point | signature | level |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |-------------|-----------|-------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `rev16` | `uint32_t rev16(uint32_t a)` | lowest-level *and* only; there is no convenience wrapper and nothing beneath it |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is exactly one exported symbol (see `SYMBOLS.md`), so the "call
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m hierarchy" is a single node and no composed pipeline exists.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Runtime options / modes / flags:** none. `rev16` takes no flag argument,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reads no global, reads no environment variable, and holds no state. There is no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m init/config/teardown call.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Compile-time configuration:** none. `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` defines no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `-D` options and `lib.c` contains no `#if`/`#ifdef`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Branches the code takes:** none — the body is four unconditional assignments
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m followed by `return`. Consequently the only axis that can change the result is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the *value* of the single argument.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Input shapes the code effectively special-cases** — all four masks
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`0xAAAA/0x5555`, `0xCCCC/0x3333`, `0xF0F0/0x0F0F`, `0xFF00/0x00FF`) are 16 bits
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m wide, so the first statement unconditionally discards bits 16..31. That splits
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the 32-bit argument into two structurally distinct halves, giving these shape
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m axes:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **low half (bits 0..15)** — fully significant; sub-shapes: zero, all-ones,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   single bit set, byte-aligned patterns, nibble-aligned patterns, alternating
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   patterns matching the mask literals, bit-reversal palindromes, arbitrary.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **high half (bits 16..31)** — entirely discarded; sub-shapes: zero, all-ones,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   arbitrary. Must never affect the result.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **whole-word interpretations** — values that differ if the 32-bit argument
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   were ever treated as signed or narrowed (`INT32_MAX`, `0x8000_0000`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `UINT32_MAX`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **cardinality of the low half** — empty (0 bits set), one (1 bit set),
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   many (2..16 bits set).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Configuration-surface table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Cross-product of {single entry point} × {the shape axes above}, pruned to the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m combinations the code actually distinguishes. Every row is exercised in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `tests/differential.rs` against BOTH `.so` objects via `libloading`, with many
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m randomized inputs per row (seeded, reproducible xorshift64* PRNG, seed
